<header class="start-masthead"><p class="eyebrow">Lab runtime · proposed documentation</p><h1>Runtime status and evidence</h1><p>Read implementation, admission, source selection and qualification as separate facts.</p><p class="source-note">Draft prepared on 2026-10-14. Integration and final T21 qualification remain pending.</p></header>

<section id="runtime-status-selected-evidence-cut" aria-labelledby="runtime-status-selected-evidence-cut-title"><h2 id="runtime-status-selected-evidence-cut-title">Selected evidence cut</h2>

<p>This draft selects public evidence available on 14 October 2026. It does not probe a live service. A later correction needs a new reviewed evidence selection, not an updated date attached to old proof.</p>

<p>The <a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-runtime/ADMISSION.md">admission overlay</a> identifies v1 as admitted by D75 while its executable remains bound to D74. The <a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-runtime/v2/REVIEW.md">v2 review</a> selects D75 as a candidate. The <a href="research/sources/docs/plans/0011-lab-runtime-completion/runs/0001-execution/T21/first-inspection-walkthrough-0001/receipt.json">fresh read-only walkthrough</a> verifies the v1 path with an absent store. Code existence, effective admission and observed behavior are reported independently.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-status-current-facts" aria-labelledby="runtime-status-current-facts-title"><h2 id="runtime-status-current-facts-title">Current facts</h2>

<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Fact</th><th scope="col">Evidence and ceiling</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>v1 read-only inspection succeeds</td><td><a href="research/sources/docs/plans/0011-lab-runtime-completion/runs/0001-execution/T21/first-inspection-walkthrough-0001/receipt.json">Three positive commands</a>, 698 sources, 468 subjects, no key/store/transaction</td></tr><tr><td>The v1 source cut is decision:0074</td><td>D75 repository admission does not silently update the executable</td></tr><tr><td>The inspected capability has admitted-current effective standing</td><td>Its raw record also retains candidate-unadmitted authoring status, draft domain lifecycle and not-observed runtime realization</td></tr><tr><td>API17 has eight reviewed overlay leaves</td><td><a href="research/sources/docs/plans/0011-lab-runtime-completion/runs/0001-execution/T02/composite-merge-preparation-0004/independent-review-0001.json">Exact applied-byte review</a>; three preimages retained, five new files, no runtime verdict</td></tr><tr><td>Old API17 e417/5c metadata is unchanged but ineligible</td><td>Changed code no longer matches that execution capture</td></tr><tr><td>Family4 is ineligible for final runtime</td><td><a href="research/sources/docs/plans/0011-lab-runtime-completion/runs/0001-execution/T02/family4-dependency-cycle-review-0001.json">Dependency-cycle diagnosis</a> and <a href="research/sources/docs/plans/0011-lab-runtime-completion/runs/0001-execution/T07/api17-task-local-capture-0004/independent-review-0001.json">flagged capture review</a></td></tr><tr><td>Paperclip reader execution was observed on 13 October</td><td><a href="research/sources/docs/plans/0010-lab-one-shot-execution/runs/0001-candidate-construction/paperclip-local-pilot-0270/closure.json">Public technical closure</a>; human pilot incomplete and old grant expired</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<p>The evidence details retain hashes and original artifacts. These facts do not combine into full34 operation qualification.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-status-failures-that-must-stay-visible" aria-labelledby="runtime-status-failures-that-must-stay-visible-title"><h2 id="runtime-status-failures-that-must-stay-visible-title">Failures that must stay visible</h2>

<p>The first walkthrough attempted to inspect implementation:cyberalchemy-lab:operational-runtime:v1. It returned unknown subject at D74 because the later D75 implementation admission is outside that cut. The corrected positive example inspects the governed-knowledge-lifecycle capability; both terminals are retained.</p>

<p>The measured learning episode reached lesson selection but expired at its original Session/Context boundary. The <a href="research/sources/docs/plans/0011-lab-runtime-completion/runs/0001-execution/T35/measurement-review-0002.json">measurement review</a> records the actual failure, cleanup and coverage limits; it contains no successful apply/assess or empirical tail calibration.</p>

<p>Family4&#x27;s Source table inherited the old API manifest and five selector files as current technical inputs. Final API publication would change those bytes. The build was stopped as an ineligible owned diagnostic; its artifacts and period remain preserved. A distinct successor must select exact historical snapshots without changing original history or weakening guards.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-status-what-would-justify-changing-this-page" aria-labelledby="runtime-status-what-would-justify-changing-this-page-title"><h2 id="runtime-status-what-would-justify-changing-this-page-title">What would justify changing this page</h2>

<p>An updated claim needs its exact selected source/profile and component bytes, actual terminal and cleanup observations, original positive/security/retry/recovery/native coverage, and an independent review. A timing-margin claim additionally needs matched real load, full-tail, instrumentation and uncertainty evidence.</p>

<p>Permanent installation, release readiness, service activation, repository admission and a human usefulness outcome each need their own evidence. Neither a pure component PASS nor a documentation build can supply them. The <a href="research/sources/docs/plans/0011-lab-runtime-completion/runs/0001-execution/T21/api-reference-preparation-0003/reference-0001/README.md">34-operation reference</a> is a historical draft from the prior capture and remains useful for declared contracts, with its qualification limits intact.</p>

</section>

